[{"sha":"3c011f27dcf57e06bbb69fcda31e6a859e4aa099","node_id":"C_kwDOEFLz89oAKDNjMDExZjI3ZGNmNTdlMDZiYmI2OWZjZGEzMWU2YTg1OWU0YWEwOTk","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/git/commits/3c011f27dcf57e06bbb69fcda31e6a859e4aa099","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/commit/3c011f27dcf57e06bbb69fcda31e6a859e4aa099","author":{"name":"Kristoffer Dalby","email":"kristoffer@dalby.cc","date":"2026-04-28T07:21:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"Kristoffer Dalby","email":"kristoffer@dalby.cc","date":"2026-04-28T07:21:17Z"},"tree":{"sha":"066987878b99fba8e76bb96f3eead13669ff8903","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/git/trees/066987878b99fba8e76bb96f3eead13669ff8903"},"message":"github: drop nu flatten in needs-more-info timer\n\nThe scheduled job has failed every night since 2026-04-13. Two\nprior fixes (race-condition guards and splitting the combined\nwhere predicate in #3200) did not address the actual cause:\n`flatten` collapses nested records in a list-of-records pipeline,\nso after `gh api ... | from json | flatten` the `label` and `user`\ncolumns no longer exist - their fields are lifted to the top\nlevel (with prefix only on naming collisions). `where label.name\n== ...` and `where user.type != \"Bot\"` then both reference a\ncolumn that is not there.\n\n`gh api --paginate` already returns a single concatenated JSON\narray, so `from json` produces a list of records directly and no\nflattening is needed. Drop both `| flatten` calls.\n\nVerified locally with nu 0.108 against the events stream of issue\n#3178: without flatten, `where event == \"labeled\" | where\nlabel.name == \"needs-more-info\" | last` returns the labeled event\nwith its `label` record intact.","parents":[{"sha":"3672a2df3a860bcb97f932d3dc7785406329b49e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/git/commits/3672a2df3a860bcb97f932d3dc7785406329b49e","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/commit/3672a2df3a860bcb97f932d3dc7785406329b49e"}],"veri